node_modules/
*.log
.DS_Store
harness/v2/.measure-sabotaged.sh

# ⛔⛔ THE DRIVER LOG'S TEMP TWIN, WHICH WAS BEING COMMITTED AND LYING TO EVERY READER.
#
# `run-batch-v2.mjs:295` writes the driver's stdout to `<record-dir>/.driver.out` purely to hand it
# to `record.mjs --log`; `record.mjs:963` then writes the CANONICAL `driver.out` beside the record.
# The temp is deleted afterwards only for verdicts outside `KEEP_LOG_VERDICTS` -- so the survivors
# were being swept into the corpus by `git add records-v2`, 733 of them.
#
# MEASURED 2026-08-30 across all 6,880 records: `driver.out` is present for 6,880 of them, and
# `.driver.out` for 733 -- of which **252 DISAGREE WITH THEIR OWN `driver.out`**. They are residue
# from an EARLIER measurement of the same package: a later re-measure rewrote `driver.out` and
# deleted its own temp on the runner, but nothing ever deletes the committed blob. 246 of the 733 sit
# on records whose verdict is not even in the keep-set, which is how you can tell.
#
# WHAT IT COST, in this repo, within minutes of being encountered: reading `.driver.out` for the 13
# `BROKEN-UNJAILED-NUB` records that carry one produced 13 logs that END IN A DIFFERENT VERDICT than
# the record beside them, and the first reading of that was "the record and its log disagree" rather
# than "this file is three days stale". The related belief that only 733 records keep a log at all --
# and so that 887 `BROKEN-WITHOUT-JAIL-TOO` causes were unknowable -- was false for the same reason.
#
# The canonical log is `driver.out` and every record has one. Nothing reads the committed `.driver.out`:
# `publish-record-v2.sh:149` reads `$STASH/rec/.driver.out` on the RUNNER, which is a different file
# in a different tree, and is unaffected by this rule.
.driver.out

# Records the publish guard refused (publish-guard.mjs). Parked OUTSIDE records-v2 so no
# bulk `git add records-v2` or whole-tree stash can sweep a withheld record into the corpus.
withheld-records/

# Written by the corpus-coverage workflow into the workspace (never /tmp — see
# harness/v2/no-inline-tmp-path.test.mjs for why a node -e body cannot carry a POSIX temp path).
coverage.json
rows.txt
